<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Interior Decision Advisor — Independent interior decision advisory' }) %></head>
<body class="landing-page">
  <header class="landing-header">
    <div class="landing-header-inner">
      <div class="landing-brand" aria-label="Interior Decision Advisor home">
        <span class="landing-brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="landing-brand-copy">
          <span class="landing-brand-name">Interior Decision Advisor</span>
          <span class="landing-brand-sub">Interior decision advisory</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <button class="landing-menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open navigation menu" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="menu-lines" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
        </span>
        <span class="menu-label">Menu</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav class="landing-menu" id="landingMenu" aria-label="Main navigation">
    <div class="landing-menu-inner">
      <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
      <a href="#pricing">Pricing</a>
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
      <a href="/advisor/cases">Dashboard</a>
    </div>
    <a class="landing-cta" href="/start">Start Your Check</a>
  </nav>

<main>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero">
      <span class="pill">Independent &middot; Not a design, interiors or contracting company</span>
      <h1>An independent advisor for your interior decisions — not just your quotations.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Interior companies sell you their solution. We help you decide what's right for you.
        Quotes from different companies rarely mean the same thing — materials, hardware, exclusions and
        commercial terms are described differently by each one, so a lower price can just mean something was
        left out. That's hard to see on your own, and generic AI tools can summarize a quote but can't call a
        company to confirm what it actually means. We can — and we're not paid by any interior company, so we
        have no reason to steer you toward one.</p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn" href="/start">Start a CHECK or VERIFY</a>
        <a class="btn outline" href="/talk-to-advisor">Talk to an Advisor</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>Help at different points in your journey</h2>
      <p class="muted small">CHECK and VERIFY (below) are our two structured, pay-online services — but they're
        not the whole business. Depending on where you are, we can also help with things like:</p>
      <ul class="small muted" style="padding-left:18px">
        <li>Independent decision consultation before you've chosen an interior company</li>
        <li>Understanding your options and the trade-offs between them</li>
        <li>Reviewing an important decision or final quotation before you sign</li>
        <li>Accompanying you to an experience centre/showroom to assess what's being shown against what's quoted</li>
        <li>Independent decision, design or communication support during the project, where appropriate</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small muted">These aren't self-service products yet — tell us what you're facing and we'll tell
        you how we can help. <a href="/talk-to-advisor">Talk to an Advisor →</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>The two services you can start online today</h2>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card service-card">
          <span class="pill">CHECK</span>
          <h3>Quote Check</h3>
          <div class="price">₹<%= SERVICES.CHECK.price.toLocaleString('en-IN') %></div>
          <p class="muted"><%= SERVICES.CHECK.blurb %></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Up to 3 quotations reviewed and compared</li>
            <li>Gaps and missing/ambiguous items flagged</li>
            <li>Written recommendation with trade-offs</li>
            <li>2–4 business day turnaround</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn outline" href="/start">Start CHECK</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card service-card">
          <span class="pill">VERIFY</span>
          <h3>Quote Verify</h3>
          <div class="price">₹<%= SERVICES.VERIFY.price.toLocaleString('en-IN') %></div>
          <p class="muted"><%= SERVICES.VERIFY.blurb %></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Everything in CHECK</li>
            <li>We call each company directly — materials, hardware, exclusions, feasibility</li>
            <li>Clarifications / revised quotes requested where needed</li>
            <li>2–4 business day turnaround</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn outline" href="/start">Start VERIFY</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section" id="how-it-works">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol class="small muted" style="padding-left:18px">
        <li>Choose CHECK or VERIFY and complete payment.</li>
        <li>Tell us about your home, budget and priorities.</li>
        <li>Upload the quotations you've received.</li>
        <li>We review (and for VERIFY, independently confirm) what's actually being offered.</li>
        <li>You get a short, plain-language report and recommendation — the decision stays yours.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section" id="pricing">
      <h2>Pricing</h2>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card service-card">
          <span class="pill">CHECK</span>
          <h3>Quote Check</h3>
          <div class="price">₹<%= SERVICES.CHECK.price.toLocaleString('en-IN') %></div>
          <p class="muted"><%= SERVICES.CHECK.blurb %></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Up to 3 quotations reviewed and compared</li>
            <li>Gaps and missing/ambiguous items flagged</li>
            <li>Written recommendation with trade-offs</li>
            <li>2–4 business day turnaround</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn outline" href="/start">Start CHECK</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card service-card">
          <span class="pill">VERIFY</span>
          <h3>Quote Verify</h3>
          <div class="price">₹<%= SERVICES.VERIFY.price.toLocaleString('en-IN') %></div>
          <p class="muted"><%= SERVICES.VERIFY.blurb %></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Everything in CHECK</li>
            <li>We call each company directly — materials, hardware, exclusions, feasibility</li>
            <li>Clarifications / revised quotes requested where needed</li>
            <li>2–4 business day turnaround</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn outline" href="/start">Start VERIFY</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section" id="about">
      <h2>Why not just compare the quotes myself?</h2>
      <p class="small muted">Interior companies quote in different formats, and cheaper often means something
        was left out — a material downgrade, an excluded item, a hidden cost. Quotation-comparison tools only
        compare line-item prices, not real scope or material equivalence. We investigate directly, disclose what
        we couldn't confirm, and never recommend a provider because they pay us — providers do not pay to be
        recommended. We're an independent advisor, not an interior contractor, architect, structural engineer,
        or a replacement for the professional actually executing your project — our role is to help you decide,
        not to design or build.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section" id="faq" style="text-align:center">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p class="muted">We are not a sales channel for interior companies. We help you understand what is really being offered and what decision you should make.</p>
      <p class="muted">Need a custom answer? <a href="/talk-to-advisor">Tell us what you need</a></p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/talk-to-advisor">Tell Us What You Need</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    const toggle = document.querySelector('.landing-menu-toggle');
    const menu = document.getElementById('landingMenu');

    if (!toggle || !menu) return;

    toggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
      const isOpen = menu.classList.toggle('open');
      toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(isOpen));
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
